    <div class="birth-header">

      <span class="birth-tag">
        THE BIRTH OF COMPASSION BRIDGE INITIATIVE UGANDA
      </span>

      <h2>

        Building Bridges of Hope

      </h2>

    </div>

    <div class="birth-content">

      <p>

        The story of Compassion Bridge Initiative Uganda is not the story of
        one individual. It is the story of compassion being passed from one
        person to another until it became a movement.

      </p>

      <p>

        Inspired by the life-changing encounter with the little boy, years of
        serving vulnerable children and communities, and the friendships built
        through the Global Compassion Coalition, a vision began to emerge.

      </p>

      <p>

        That vision was simple but profound:

      </p>

      <div class="vision-box">

        <h3>

          To restore dignity, create opportunities and build resilient
          communities where every person can live with hope.

        </h3>

      </div>

      <p>

        From that vision, Compassion Bridge Initiative Uganda was established.

      </p>

      <p>

        Today, the organisation works alongside communities to improve access
        to quality education, empower widows and vulnerable women, strengthen
        livelihoods, promote health, develop vocational skills, protect
        vulnerable children and respond compassionately to the needs of
        communities across Uganda.

      </p>

      <p>

        Every programme we implement, every partnership we build and every
        child we support reflects the same lesson that began with one
        half-eaten apple:

      </p>

      <blockquote>

        Compassion has the power to change lives.

      </blockquote>

      <p>

        We believe that lasting transformation begins when ordinary people
        choose to care for one another.

      </p>

    </div>

  </div>

